Requirement Description:
1.    CURRENT CONDITION:

Building 568 is affected by water leak issues, mostly from the roof in the eastern part. The roof (1500 sq. m) has been repaired many times and currently we can find four different types of insulation. Many devices are currently installed on the roof terrace. With a recent contract (JOC T.O. N3319122F4364 – see attached RFO 2-4364) only an approx. 100 sq. m roof portion has been repaired. 

The restrooms of the Liberty Center, the western block of the building, are in poor conditions and require a renovation.

The Facility is served by 3 different HVAC systems, each one dedicated to a specific space (Liberty Center, Big Al, Jox), the chiller unit serving Big Al spaces is operating even with an increasing number of trouble-calls, mostly related to chiller regulation and control.



2.    REQUIREMENT: 

•    BASE - Repair the entire roof, restore façade plaster and repaint it;

•    OPTION 1 - Renovate the restrooms at Liberty Center;

•    OPTION 2 - Replace #1 chiller unit serving Big Al;



3.    DESCRIPTION OF WORK:



BASE REQUIREMENT

In order to repair the roof:

•    Disconnect and remove the existing equipment on the roof;

•    Remove the entire waterproof membrane, including the insulation layer, the perimeter metal flashing and the downspouts;

•    Assess and verify the existing roof slope layer;

•    Install new insulation layer and waterproof membrane;

•    Install new downspouts inlets

•    Reinstall existing equipment on the roof;



In order to repair the façade:

•    Disconnect and remove the existing equipment on the façade;

•    Perform plaster restoration where needed;

•     ...

NOTE: description has been truncated, please see Project Note for full description.

